Switch expressions(case X -> {})
will now be used as a statement as well as expressions.
This makes code simplification and pattern matching possible for the switch.

old way:
DayOfWeek dayOfWeek = LocalDate.now().getDayOfWeek();
String typeOfDay = "";
switch (dayOfWeek) {
    case MONDAY:
    case TUESDAY:
    case WEDNESDAY:
    case THURSDAY:
    case FRIDAY:
        typeOfDay = "Working Day";
        break;
    case SATURDAY:
    case SUNDAY:
        typeOfDay = "Day Off";
}

new way:
typeOfDay = switch (dayOfWeek) {
 case MONDAY, TUESDAY, WEDNESDAY, THURSDAY, FRIDAY -> "Working Day";
 case SATURDAY, SUNDAY -> "Day Off";
};
✅ No need for break

✅ Cleaner, more readable

✅ switch can return a value (used as an expression)
